    <section id="why" class="thinking wrap section-space" aria-labelledby="thinking-title">
      <div class="section-label" data-mint-reveal><span>01 /</span><p>OUR THINKING</p></div>
      <div class="thinking-intro" data-mint-reveal><h2 id="thinking-title">A faster world.<br><em>A more thoughtful you.</em></h2><div class="thinking-body"><p>AI is making it easier to turn ideas into action. Deciding what matters — and what to do next — still calls for human judgement.</p><p>We believe that judgement grows from the things we notice, the patterns we recognise, and the questions we keep asking. A little practice, often, can give us more to draw on.</p></div></div>
      <div class="principles">
        <article data-mint-reveal><div class="principle-top"><span>01</span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 90" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 45h88M60 8v74"/><circle cx="60" cy="45" r="29"/><circle cx="60" cy="45" r="17"/><circle cx="60" cy="45" r="4" fill="currentColor"/></svg></div><h3>Notice the difference.</h3><p>A flag. A shape. A familiar detail seen afresh. Learning starts when something makes you look a little closer.</p></article>
        <article data-mint-reveal><div class="principle-top"><span>02</span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 90" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="60" cy="45" rx="45" ry="16" transform="rotate(-35 60 45)"/><ellipse cx="60" cy="45" rx="45" ry="16" transform="rotate(35 60 45)"/><ellipse cx="60" cy="45" rx="45" ry="16" transform="rotate(90 60 45)"/><circle cx="60" cy="45" r="4" fill="currentColor"/></svg></div><h3>Build an instinct.</h3><p>Come back to an idea. Compare it with another. Repetition helps turn unfamiliar information into something you recognise.</p></article>
        <article data-mint-reveal><div class="principle-top"><span>03</span><svg viewBox="0 0 120 90" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 45c20-48 40-48 50 0s30 48 50 0M10 45c20 48 40 48 50 0s30-48 50 0M10 45h100"/><circle cx="60" cy="45" r="4" fill="currentColor"/></svg></div><h3>Make room for curiosity.</h3><p>No grand study plan needed. Just a few questions in an ordinary moment, and a reason to come back tomorrow.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>
